<p class="sst-lead">Two problems sit underneath every application.</p>

<div class="sst-frag">
  <p><strong>Challenge 1 &mdash; Measure or simulate, then segment.</strong> Get clean boundary curves out of
  noisy imagery (xCT, SEM, EBSD). Garbage segmentation, garbage shape.</p>
</div>

<div class="sst-frag">
  <p><strong>Challenge 2 &mdash; Is this the same as that, and if not, why?</strong></p>
  <blockquote>Are the shapes in one image, <em>up to rigid motions</em>, the same? If not, are the differences
  due to <strong>scale</strong> (linear deformation) or <strong>undulation</strong> (nonlinear deformation)?</blockquote>
</div>

<div class="sst-frag">
  <p class="sst-claim">SST answers Challenge 2 with a decision that is <em>explainable</em> &mdash; it tells you
  <em>which</em> kind of difference it found &mdash; with no labels and across thousands of shapes.</p>
</div>
